    "title": "US Moves to Curb Remote Access to Nvidia's Advanced AI Chips",
    "type": "policy",
    "detail": "Commerce Department (BIS) issued an interim final rule on Nov 16, 2026 requiring federal licenses before advanced AI chips or servers are sent to foreign data centers serving clients in China or other restricted countries, closing the cloud remote-access loophole; licensing also extends to chip shipments to Indonesia, Malaysia, Singapore, Thailand and Brazil. Context: the Megaspeed case. Legal-authority questions remain (Remote Access Security Act not yet law).",
